    "html": "<p>A pendulum of length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span> oscillates with simple harmonic motion (SHM) on Earth. The pendulum passes through its equilibrium position <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60\"></span> times per minute. When the pendulum is taken to Planet X, its period of oscillation is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8.0\"></span> s. What is the best estimate for the value of the gravitational acceleration on Planet X?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.16\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.63\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.3\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
